tip: | Look at one tile. | This diamond is 24 pixels wide and 12 tall: always 2 across for 1 down. Everything on the path stands on this shape. Tap the stages, then Finished.
tip: 1 | Draw the diamond first. | The edges climb in runs of 2 pixels, never smoother. That stair is what lets tiles lock together. One flat color is enough to check it.
tip: 4 | Keep texture off the border. | The tufts stay a pixel or two inside the edge, so the seam between two tiles has nothing to line up.
tip: | Now repeat it. | The preview lays this tile out 3 x 3. Look for a line or a shape that gives the tile away. The outline is left out there, because tiles in a floor touch. | | seam 0 0
